WEBVTT

00:00:00.173 --> 00:00:04.737
{happy}Hello, and a very warm welcome to Shah Spectrum.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:05.678
If you're new here, welcome.

00:00:05.678 --> 00:00:11.533
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us once more.

00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:14.872
Last week, the price of oil fell by about a sixth.

00:00:14.872 --> 00:00:18.963
One report called it the biggest weekly drop since 2020.

00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:23.360
So why is petrol at your pump priced exactly as it was in May?

00:00:24.055 --> 00:00:24.995
Hi, I'm Mittal Shah.

00:00:24.995 --> 00:00:30.686
Stay with me for a few minutes, and the gap between the headline and the pump will

00:00:30.686 --> 00:00:31.707
make sense.

00:00:31.707 --> 00:00:33.627
{fluent}First, what happened.

00:00:33.627 --> 00:00:39.247
Brent, the global benchmark price for crude oil, dipped below ninety dollars a

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:42.058
barrel on Tuesday, the tenth of November.

00:00:42.058 --> 00:00:44.604
That is the first time since August.

00:00:44.604 --> 00:00:47.995
It was a dip during trading, not a closing price.

00:00:47.995 --> 00:00:52.018
And it is nearly a quarter lower than the peak of late October.

00:00:52.898 --> 00:00:54.187
Why did it fall?

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:58.325
Analysts link it to hopes that the fighting with Iran is easing.

00:00:58.325 --> 00:01:03.796
Reports said President Trump was not planning to attack Iran at this point, and

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.700
there are hopes of talks mediated by Qatar.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:11.359
Ship traffic through the Strait of Hormuz has also picked up, and one analyst says

00:01:11.359 --> 00:01:15.377
crude oil flows have almost returned to pre-war levels.

00:01:15.377 --> 00:01:20.650
That is the narrow channel that carries about a fifth of the world's oil in normal

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.250
times.

00:01:21.152 --> 00:01:23.412
Oil is priced on expectation.

00:01:23.412 --> 00:01:27.254
If buyers expect more oil tomorrow, they pay less today.

00:01:28.226 --> 00:01:29.580
Now to the pump.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:35.219
In India, petrol and diesel prices are set by the fuel retailers, the oil marketing

00:01:35.219 --> 00:01:38.267
companies, and they do not follow oil day by day.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:43.315
They raised prices four times in May, and have not changed them since.

00:01:43.315 --> 00:01:46.220
No company has announced a change this week.

00:01:46.956 --> 00:01:47.850
Why not cut now?

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.968
Look at what they paid.

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:54.886
The Indian basket, which is the mix of crude India actually buys, averaged nearly

00:01:54.886 --> 00:01:58.736
one hundred and twenty dollars a barrel in October.

00:01:58.736 --> 00:02:03.066
In the first days of November it was still above one hundred.

00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:08.857
So the retailers have been losing money on fuel sales, and reports say those losses

00:02:08.857 --> 00:02:09.901
are now easing.

00:02:10.678 --> 00:02:13.832
Here is why India feels this more than most.

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:20.219
It imports about eighty-eight per cent of its crude, close to nine of every ten

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:20.819
barrels.

00:02:20.744 --> 00:02:23.636
One report gives a rule of thumb.

00:02:23.636 --> 00:02:29.944
Every ten dollars off the price of crude cuts the country's current account deficit

00:02:29.944 --> 00:02:32.476
by about fifteen billion dollars a year.

00:02:32.476 --> 00:02:37.769
The current account deficit is the difference between what a country pays the rest

00:02:37.769 --> 00:02:39.642
of the world and what it earns from it.

00:02:39.642 --> 00:02:43.238
A smaller deficit eases pressure on the rupee.

00:02:43.238 --> 00:02:48.457
That is a likely effect, not a promise, and it depends on the price staying down.

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:50.886
What do we not know?

00:02:50.886 --> 00:02:53.617
Talks are hoped for, not agreed.

00:02:53.617 --> 00:02:59.383
Houthi attacks on Saudi energy sites are continuing, and liquefied natural gas and

00:02:59.383 --> 00:03:01.575
refined fuels are still constrained.

00:03:01.575 --> 00:03:07.700
Different reports give slightly different prices for the same day, because the

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.326
market moves by the hour.

00:03:09.326 --> 00:03:13.115
So treat ninety dollars as a moment, not a new level.

00:03:14.211 --> 00:03:15.641
To sum up:

00:03:15.641 --> 00:03:17.007
oil has fallen fast on hope, not on a deal.

00:03:17.007 --> 00:03:23.507
India's pump prices have not moved, and the retailers are still recovering what

00:03:23.507 --> 00:03:24.347
crude cost them.

00:03:24.347 --> 00:03:27.709
And the benefit to India is real only if the fall lasts.

00:03:28.464 --> 00:03:31.512
Before you go, here is earlier background.

00:03:31.512 --> 00:03:37.356
On the twenty-ninth of October, our episode 'Hormuz and oil:

00:03:37.356 --> 00:03:39.685
what it means for India' explained why the strait matters.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:43.863
And on the fifth of November, 'US midterms aftermath:

00:03:43.863 --> 00:03:49.097
oil, shares and India' looked at oil, shares and the rupee after the vote.

00:03:49.097 --> 00:03:51.449
The links are in the description.

00:03:51.449 --> 00:03:55.102
{happy}Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode!

